<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramesses XI</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1070 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramesses XI was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/twentieth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twentieth Dynasty</a> and of the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>. During his reign real power passed to the high priests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a> and to military commanders. His death around 1070 BCE ended the New Kingdom through administrative dissolution rather than conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramesses-xi.jpg" alt="Ramesses XI" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Richard Lepsius (1810-84) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Temple_Khonsu_Ramesses_XI_Lepsius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
